<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kolon wins $300mln Thai power plant deal.</title>
<headline>Kolon wins $300mln Thai power plant deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Kolon Construction Co said on Tuesday a consortium led by the company had won a $300 million order to build a power plant for Thailand's Siam Power Generation Co.</p>
<p>Kolon has a 72 percent stake in the consortium and France's European Gas Turbines S.A. the rest, a company spokeswoman said.  </p>
<p>A Kolon statement said the construction of the 450 megawatt thermal power unit, won on a turn-key basis, was due to start this month for completion in June 2000.</p>
<p>The plant will be fuelled by gas, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
